                    <h2>Practice Exercises</h2>
                    
                    <div class="exercise-box">
                        <h4>Exercise 2.1: Personal Greeting</h4>
                        <p>Create a program that asks for the user's name and favorite color, then displays a personalized message.</p>
                        <p><strong>Expected output:</strong></p>
                        <pre><code class="language-bash">What is your name? Sarah
What is your favorite color? Blue
Nice to meet you, Sarah! Blue is a great color!</code></pre>
                    </div>

                    <div class="exercise-box">
                        <h4>Exercise 2.2: Simple Calculator Setup</h4>
                        <p>Create a program that asks the user for two numbers, then displays both numbers back to them. (We'll add the actual calculation in a future lesson!)</p>
                        <p><strong>Hint:</strong> You can store the input as strings for now.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="exercise-box">
                        <h4>Exercise 2.3: ASCII Art</h4>
                        <p>Create a program that displays ASCII art using multiple <code>Console.WriteLine()</code> statements. Try making a simple shape or your initials!</p>
                        <p><strong>Example:</strong></p>
                        <pre><code class="language-bash">  *  
 * * 
*****
 * * 
 * * </code></pre>
                    </div>
